repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Society-of-actuaries-research-institute/ML281-AI-and-Individual-Life-Insurance-Challenge-Pramod-Misra
abstract: >-
  Reproduction code for the Society of Actuaries ML281 AI and Individual Life
  Insurance Challenge submission, selected for publication following review
  committee comment and a revised resubmission. Using the SOA Individual Life
  Experience Committee (ILEC) 2012-2019 experience study, the work tests whether
  machine learning improves on the VBT 2015 mortality table for individual life
  insurance. It finds that out of time the static table forecasts better than the
  machine-learned models tested; that a gradient-boosted model is not merely
  relearning the table; that differences between model classes sit inside
  fold-to-fold noise; and that formulating the problem as a count model with a VBT
  log-offset gives the best-calibrated result. The repository contains the
  analysis notebook, the verified data path, the published figures, and a numeric
  ledger tying every reported value to the file that produced it.
keywords:
  - actuarial science
  - mortality modelling
  - life insurance
  - machine learning
  - gradient boosting
  - reproducible research
  - ILEC
  - VBT 2015
